<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ied64203035592fa3ef050cbe536c639b6965ac16" commit="5a17d98ee5091423ac7441eb0f2d2cae8cf1e06d" commit_message="login: Unregister suspend delays when ARC stops  This implementation was leaking suspend delays, so powerd would often wait for suspend delay IDs that were no longer being used to report readiness after e.g. the ARC instance crashed and registered another suspend delay. This meant suspends could take up to 20 seconds.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58560 TEST=crash container, look at logs, unit tests  Change-Id: Ied64203035592fa3ef050cbe536c639b6965ac16 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399979 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399979" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/79/399979/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia560fd627e010635719b6e584e90a1a6fe53ab54" commit="8871c3ce19fb86497690ed842c091cdedb8abd5b" commit_message="login: fix ARC instance freezer state path  This was moved, which meant session_manager was spewing some more warnings into the logs than usual, but also that the ARC instance wasn't being correctly frozen and thawed across suspends.  BUG=None TEST=start instance, suspend/resume, check /var/log/messages   to ensure session_manager does not display any warnings trying   to change the instance freezer state  Change-Id: Ia560fd627e010635719b6e584e90a1a6fe53ab54 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399965 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399965" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/65/399965/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5ba43d9e56f0f25aefe30f1ca1bd7fed602abde0" commit="8554defed3cffdf3623649dbc0aca281d49485d2" commit_message="CRAS: Add files to .gitignore found during development.  Add a few files commonly found in the adhd directory or one of it's sub-directories during development (eg: after cros_workon_make --test adhd).  BUG=None TEST=N/A  Change-Id: I5ba43d9e56f0f25aefe30f1ca1bd7fed602abde0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391050 Commit-Ready: John Muir &lt;muirj@google.com&gt; Tested-by: John Muir &lt;muirj@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="391050" owner_email="muirj@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/50/391050/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0b1d96457d98601643da6516c0cf15ff2af351b1" commit="843e6010bccd1e0388099fd74183dc5aabb3f119" commit_message="CRAS client: Start stream audio thread before connection  When the server sends the first data request to the client, it is important that the client is ready to respond instantly. This change ensures that this is the case by starting the stream's audio thread before the connection to the server has been established. If there is a problem with the server then the audio thread is stopped as per normal.  BUG=None TEST=Unit tests updated.      Audio playback works on new device.      Audio playback and capture work on Samus.  Change-Id: I0b1d96457d98601643da6516c0cf15ff2af351b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387135 Commit-Ready: John Muir &lt;muirj@google.com&gt; Tested-by: John Muir &lt;muirj@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="387135" owner_email="muirj@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/35/387135/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3a4a03e4b300240a167e1fbc3eb3e23c55551c8b" commit="e22c685ae31ea34f37013bf30b14dc8b977d64b2" commit_message="minigbm: i915: enable required Android buffers  The Play Store wants a HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBA_8888 (ABGR with fourcc) buffer with the 0x8933 flag sometimes, which translates to:  GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_READ_OFTEN | GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_WRITE_OFTEN | GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_TEXTURE | GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER | GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_FB | GRALLOC_USAGE_CURSOR  Some dEQP EGL tests also need XBGR8888 buffers with GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_WRITE_OFTEN | GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_READ_OFTEN flags.  In addition, we need to support YUV buffers with these usage flags:  GRALLOC_USAGE_EXTERNAL_DISP | GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER | GRALLOC_USAGE_TEXTURE  for Youtube videos to work, so add that too.  BUG=chromium:616275 TEST=Play Angry birds and run Youtube app on Cyan.  Verified all dEQP EGL tests pass:  run cts --package com.drawelements.deqp.egl  CQ-DEPEND=CL:392546  Change-Id: I3a4a03e4b300240a167e1fbc3eb3e23c55551c8b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/392547 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="392547" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/47/392547/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8dbd989f2638c99200866f8191450c71114bdbe5" commit="e7183941dc08fc5343e6928e3a3f645450913fef" commit_message="minigbm: rockchip: enable NV12 for Android  For NV12 buffers to work on Android, we need to use the same logic that we use in gralloc_drm_rockchip.  Otherwise, video playback doesn't work in the container.  BUG=chromium:616275 TEST=Play Youtube app.  Also ran plane_test (which defaults to NV12). CQ-DEPEND=CL:392547  Change-Id: I8dbd989f2638c99200866f8191450c71114bdbe5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/392548 Commit-Ready: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="392548" owner_email="gurchetansingh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/48/392548/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I406c44706f90973ddbb79d59a74ddb194224debc" commit="7ca300adcad963a3d6ea8b495563d7f69afc7479" commit_message="login: Clean up for session_manager_impl and its test.  session_manager had a variation to build a second argument of TriggerImpulse(). With this CL, inlined initializer list is used if possible.  SetDefaultMockBehavior() is introduced to the unittest. Some redundant invocation is migrated into the function.  BUG=None TEST=Ran unittests.  Change-Id: I406c44706f90973ddbb79d59a74ddb194224debc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/395467 Commit-Ready: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hidehiko Abe &lt;hidehiko@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="395467" owner_email="hidehiko@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/67/395467/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Ia1fa28971c65d7d0639966e715f742309245172b" commit="446f08a29a73fb50e7ba02b195865ba628b6b8ee" commit_message="rk3399: Reserve enough framebuffer memory for 32bpp hires panels  Some of our RK3399 devices have panel resolutions as high as 2400x1600. With 16bpp that barely still fit into an 8MB framebuffer, but then we changed it to 32bpp for better image quality...  Note that this is a band-aid. Coreboot-allocated framebuffers shouldn't be used at all on ARM64 devices, since libpayload is perfectly capable to dynamically allocate it with the right size based on EDID-information on this architecture. That will require some more elaborate work to be fixed with later patches.  BRANCH=gru BUG=chrome-os-partner:58044 TEST=Warm-reboot Kevin on the dev screen, confirm that you don't see the lower half of the screen that overflowed our allocated framebuffer preserved from the last boot as soon as the backlight turns on.  Change-Id: Ia1fa28971c65d7d0639966e715f742309245172b Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399966 Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399966" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/66/399966/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I870dd7cd0253fb8474138bd305faf69d6e5661de" commit="ac3cfcce6ee4f051868669068cdad3f3a1f60e65" commit_message="service_constants: Add Flags property to bluetooth_device  Add the name of the Advertising Data Flags property for remote devices in BlueZ.  BUG=chromium:618442 TEST=emerge system_api  Change-Id: I870dd7cd0253fb8474138bd305faf69d6e5661de Signed-off-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/398418 Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaturvedi &lt;rkc@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="398418" owner_email="puthik@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/18/398418/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib2179454ad320fe2bd2787d79f4783ec2a6b9784" commit="9ba69330044178179746aa8de087030ff8286e07" commit_message="cros-kernel2: remove fragment for tegradrm  BUG=chromium:478339 CQ-DEPEND=CL:399619 TEST=build_packages --board nyan_big  Change-Id: Ib2179454ad320fe2bd2787d79f4783ec2a6b9784 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399602 Commit-Ready: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399602" owner_email="hshi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/02/399602/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8907.0.0-rc4"/></manifest>